  "summary": "Eight published items and one preprint (2026-10-01) pair skeletal muscle aging single-cell work with proteomic and multimodal biomarkers of mortality.",
  "synthesis": "Activity centers on aging biology tied to mortality and tissue decline. Single-myofibre multi-omics in ICU-acquired weakness links an inflammatory fibre state to myosin energetics, while a review frames skeletal muscle aging as multicellular coordination failure across stem, stromal, immune, vascular, and neuromuscular compartments. A UK Biobank deep-learning SASP score from plasma proteomics predicts mortality and chronic disease, and LBC1936 benchmarks proteomic organ clocks against other ageing biomarkers for 16-year all-cause mortality. A vervet preprint connects miRNA-mRNA networks to age-related gait decline. Mosaic chromosome Y loss, with single-cell monocyte and macrophage evidence, associates with incident AMD in 223,051 men. The rise ratio of 1.71 is recorded alongside eight published items and one preprint; no code or industry items appear.",
